{"name":"Electric Orchid","hex":"#cd00fe","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"electric","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, produced by, operated with, or utilising electricity; electrical.","Of or relating to an electronic version of a musical instrument that has an acoustic equivalent."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electricity; the electricity supply.","An electric powered version of something that was originally or is more commonly not electric.\n An electric car, locomotive, train etc.\n\nAn electric toothbrush.\n\nAn electric typewriter."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electric"},{"term":"orchid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the orchid family (Orchidaceae), bearing unusually-shaped flowers of beautiful colours. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A light bluish-red, violet-red or purple colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a light purple colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orchid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Electricity","blocks":[{"text":"Electricity is the set of physical phenomena associated with the presence and motion of matter possessing an electric charge. Electricity is related to magnetism, both being part of the phenomenon of electromagnetism, as described by Maxwell's equations. Common phenomena are related to electricity, including lightning, static electricity, electric heating, electric discharges and many others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/London_MMB_%C2%BB1E6_Lightning.jpg/330px-London_MMB_%C2%BB1E6_Lightning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electricity"},{"title":"Orchid","blocks":[{"text":"Orchids are plants that belong to the family Orchidaceae, a diverse and widespread group of flowering plants with blooms that are often colourful and fragrant. Orchids are cosmopolitan plants, living in diverse habitats on every continent except Antarctica. The world's richest diversity of orchid genera and species is in the tropics. Many species are epiphytes, living on trees. The flowers and their pollination mechanisms are highly specialized, attracting insect pollinators by colour, pattern, scent, pheromones, and sometimes by mimicking female insects. Orchids have very small seeds, relying on fungal partners for germination. Some orchids have no leaves, either photosynthesizing with their roots or relying entirely on fungal partners for food."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg/330px-Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchid"},{"title":"Orchid (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Orchid is a bright rich purple color that resembles the color which various orchids often exhibit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Labiata.jpg/330px-Labiata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchid_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Thales.jpg/330px-Thales.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Thales.jpg/330px-Thales.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A fictional portrait of Thales, the earliest known researcher into electricity","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThales.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Franklin-Benjamin-LOC.jpg/500px-Franklin-Benjamin-LOC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Franklin-Benj